- op: discuss  # dc9e
  at: '2026-09-18T23:26:12Z'  # dc9e
  by: agent  # dc9e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dc9e
  clock: 3  # dc9e
  nonce: dc9e  # dc9e
  message: "Precondition landed (WI-juzig, PR #1065): `languages` is now a gated declaration in the taxonomy vocabulary, and `backend` is set on 4 of 118 (rust=\"tree-sitter\", rust_analyzer=\"scip\", make=\"tree-sitter\", manifest_targets=\"regex\") — was 0. The registry can now enumerate \"languages claimed by >1 analyzer\": rust -> [rust, rust_analyzer]; svelte -> [svelte, javascript]; vue -> [vue, javascript]. NOTE for the contract's registry test (\"every analyzer whose languages overlap another's declares a merge anchor\"): the javascript/svelte/vue overlap is NOT two backends for one language (the js analyzer reads the <script> block, the svelte/vue analyzers the template) — a distinct-backend rule would misfire there; the anchor must be declared, not inferred from backend inequality. New helper: registry.analyzers_for_language(). One consumer-side finding: five bridge linkers' depends_on had named only the incumbent rust producer; now name both — the contract should say what depends_on means under multiple producers."  # dc9e
